msgid "Accepted per round"
msgstr "Accettati per ciclo"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:176
msgid "31B (dense, 18.4 GB read per token)"
msgstr "31B (denso, 18,4 GB letti per token)"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:177
msgid "14.9 tok/s"
msgstr "14.9 tok/s"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:178
msgid "**31.0 tok/s** (2.1x)"
msgstr "**31.0 tok/s** (2.1x)"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:179
msgid "2.08 of 4"
msgstr "2,08 su 4"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:180
msgid "26B-A4B (MoE, ~2.2 GB read per token)"
msgstr "26B-A4B (MoE, ~2,2 GB letti per token)"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:181
msgid "73.2 tok/s"
msgstr "73.2 tok/s"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:182
msgid "65.9 tok/s (0.9x)"
msgstr "65.9 tok/s (0.9x)"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:183
msgid "1.40 of 4"
msgstr "1,40 su 4"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:185
msgid ""
"The 0.83 GB drafter costs about 5% of a 31B decoding step but 39% of a "
"26B-A4B one, so on the MoE the three drafting steps of a round already "
"exceed one plain decoding step — and the round has to win that back from a "
"lower acceptance rate. The MoE is still the faster model here in absolute "
"terms; it simply has no headroom left for speculation."
msgstr ""
"Il draft da 0,83 GB costa circa il 5% di un passo 31B, ma il 39% di un passo"
" 26B-A4B. Su MoE, tre passi draft superano già un passo normale e devono "
"compensarlo con accettazione inferiore. MoE resta più veloce in termini "
"assoluti, ma senza margine per la speculazione."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:191
msgid ""
"So measure before leaving it on, and note that the verification step itself "
"is not the problem: a four-token forward costs only ~40% more than a single-"
"token one on either model."
msgstr ""
"Misurare prima di lasciarlo attivo. La verifica non è il problema: un "
"forward di quattro token costa solo circa il 40% in più di uno di un token "
"su entrambi i modelli."
